# Stock Analysis Project

- Project root: `/Users/keith/Documents/stock-analysis/`
- Run analysis: `source .venv/bin/activate && python src/main.py SYMBOL`
- Do not commit `.venv/` or large CSV caches
- Data source: yfinance (free, delayed) — not for live trading
- Before quoting financial figures, search `data/raw/{SYMBOL}/` and validate its
  manifests with `python scripts/validate_raw_manifests.py --root data/raw`
- For symbols in `config/official_sources.yaml`, also require
  `--coverage-config config/official_sources.yaml`; inspect `pending_sources`
  and `unavailable_sources` before calling a six-quarter package complete
- Source priority: regulatory filing / official IR > official presentation >
  third-party research > yfinance; never let an aggregator override an official figure
- Treat `source_tier: unverified` as a research lead, not authoritative evidence
- State fiscal period, currency, accounting basis, source, and validation status
  for material financial figures; stop the verdict if a critical figure is disputed
- Never expose or index files under `~/Documents/stock-analysis-private/`
- User-facing summaries: Traditional Chinese
- Reports must include disclaimer: research only, not investment advice
- Extend modules in `src/` — keep `main.py` as thin CLI orchestrator
- Handoff: GitHub only; one Skill per run; follow `AGENTS.md`. Claude Cowork
  follows `CLAUDE.md` (review memos, no parallel unpushed edits)
- User-facing HTML only in `docs/`; run `python scripts/publish_html_reports.py`;
  deliver a GitHub Pages URL, never source code
- Mac keeps the full file archive (git + OneDrive `data/raw`); do not treat the
  cloud reconstruct as a replacement for the local copy
